    "text": "Let the first three terms $2, p$ and $q$, with $q \\neq 2$, of a G.P. be respectively the $7^{\\text {th }}, 8^{\\text {th }}$ and $13^{\\text {th }}$ terms of an A.P. If the $5^{\\text {th }}$ term of the G.P. is the $n^{\\text {th }}$ term of the A.P., then $n$ is equal to:"
